<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 81 0 R/T(My version opens the file with a with statement, so it is always closed, even after an error. It reads one line at a time, so memory stays almost constant \(about 21 KB measured\) instead of holding all 50,000 lines \(about 5 MB with read\(\)\). Specific exceptions handle only expected data problems; real programming bugs still appear. Decimal keeps paise exact, so totals are correct. Blank and damaged lines are skipped and logged with line numbers, so no bill is lost silently. The file name is a parameter, so one function serves every month. \(94 words\) )/E(My version opens the file with a with statement, so it is always closed, even after an error. It reads one line at a time, so memory stays almost constant \(about 21 KB measured\) instead of holding all 50,000 lines \(about 5 MB with read\(\)\). Specific exceptions handle only expected data problems; real programming bugs still appear. Decimal keeps paise exact, so totals are correct. Blank and damaged lines are skipped and logged with line numbers, so no bill is lost silently. The file name is a parameter, so one function serves every month. \(94 words\) )/Pg 11 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

