<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 88 0 R/T(Why the error is hidden: NameError is a subclass of Exception, so the broad clause catches it, and pass discards it. The program continues and returns a wrong number as if nothing happened - the worst kind of failure, because wrong attendance would be reported with confidence. Specific clauses catch only the errors the programmer expects; unexpected ones \(including typos\) still stop the program and show a traceback. )/E(Why the error is hidden: NameError is a subclass of Exception, so the broad clause catches it, and pass discards it. The program continues and returns a wrong number as if nothing happened - the worst kind of failure, because wrong attendance would be reported with confidence. Specific clauses catch only the errors the programmer expects; unexpected ones \(including typos\) still stop the program and show a traceback. )/Pg 18 0 R/K[16]>>
endobj

