903 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 91 0 R/T(Time: both versions are O\(n\) for n lines/bytes processed; the with statement does exactly what try/finally does \(it calls __exit__, which closes the file\), so the measured per-call times \(about 9-10 microseconds\) are the same within noise. Space: unchanged, O\(1\) extra. Open files after an error: with the with version, 0 files remain open \(each is closed on exit\). With manual try/finally, 0 remain open only if every open\(\) is placed correctly \(nested so each file has its own finally\); if the second open\(\) is written outside protection, 1 file remains open - and with n files opened carelessly, up to n. The with version gives this protection by construction, which is why it is preferred. )/E(Time: both versions are O\(n\) for n lines/bytes processed; the with statement does exactly what try/finally does \(it calls __exit__, which closes the file\), so the measured per-call times \(about 9-10 microseconds\) are the same within noise. Space: unchanged, O\(1\) extra. Open files after an error: with the with version, 0 files remain open \(each is closed on exit\). With manual try/finally, 0 remain open only if every open\(\) is placed correctly \(nested so each file has its own finally\); if the second open\(\) is written outside protection, 1 file remains open - and with n files opened carelessly, up to n. The with version gives this protection by construction, which is why it is preferred. )/Pg 21 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

