<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 103 0 R/T(From n=1000 to n = 8000 \(8 times more data\) the list time grew about 34 times \(0.0046s to 0.158 s\), the quadraticpattern, while the set time grew only about 9 times \(0.00009 s to 0.0008 s\), roughly linear; at n = 8000 theset was about 200 times faster. Both need O\(n\) space, so the set trades a modest amount of memoryfor a large saving of time. For one fest with a few hundred students both work, but the set remainssafe if registrations grow. )/E(From n=1000 to n = 8000 \(8 times more data\) the list time grew about 34 times \(0.0046s to 0.158 s\), the quadraticpattern, while the set time grew only about 9 times \(0.00009 s to 0.0008 s\), roughly linear; at n = 8000 theset was about 200 times faster. Both need O\(n\) space, so the set trades a modest amount of memoryfor a large saving of time. For one fest with a few hundred students both work, but the set remainssafe if registrations grow. )/Pg 33 0 R/K[6]>>
