2630 0 obj
<</Title(Why the error is hidden: NameError is a subclass of Exception, so the broad clause catches it, and pass discards it. The program continues and returns a wrong number as if nothing happened - the worst kind of failure, because wrong attendance would be reported with confidence. Specific clauses catch only the errors the programmer expects; unexpected ones \(including typos\) still stop the program and show a traceback.)/Dest[18 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2610 0 R>>
endobj

