2719 0 obj
<</Title(Time: both versions are O\(n\) for n lines/bytes processed; the with statement does exactly what try/finally does \(it calls __exit__, which closes the file\), so the measured per-call times \(about 9-10 microseconds\) are the same within noise. Space: unchanged, O\(1\) extra. Open files after an error: with the with version, 0 files remain open \(each is closed on exit\). With manual try/finally, 0 remain open only if every open\(\) is placed correctly \(nested so each file has its own finally\); if the second open\(\) is written outside protection, 1 file remains open - and with n files opened carelessly, up to n. The with version gives this protection by construction, which is why it is preferred.)/Dest[21 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 2700 0 R/Next 2738 0 R>>
endobj

2720 0 obj
<</Title(them, creating module objects\); the measured warm import was under 1 ms. Modules are then stored in sys.modules, so a second import costs only a dictionary lookup \(about 2-4 microseconds measured\). Measured here: about 0.4 ms for the script and 0.9 ms for the package.)/Dest[26 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 2739 0 R/Next 2701 0 R>>
endobj

